WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 065. ONE SESSION IS NOT THE SYSTEM. A fixed synthetic session sits inside a longer pathway of preparation, follow-up, integration, referrals, supports, and accountable handoffs.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
EXPAND THE RECORD. CONTINUITY HAS MORE THAN ONE STEP. Keep the session connected to declared purpose, permission state, handoff acceptance, follow-up ownership, due state, evidence, and recourse.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
KEEP FAILURES DISTINCT. UNACCEPTED · WITHDRAWN · OVERDUE. Do not flatten an unaccepted handoff, withdrawn permission, or overdue follow-up into one generic status.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
BOUND THE SYSTEM. A PATHWAY IS NOT A LIFELINE. This synthetic fixture does not monitor, diagnose, triage, treat, determine consent validity, or provide emergency response.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
MAKE RESPONSIBILITY VISIBLE. THE CARE DOES NOT END WHEN THE SESSION DOES. The sender retains declared responsibility until acceptance; owners, due states, evidence, and exception routes stay visible.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. OWNERSHIP CONTINUES. A CONTINUITY RECORD IS USEFUL WHEN THE NEXT STEP, OWNER, PERMISSION, EVIDENCE, RECOURSE, AND LIMIT REMAIN CONNECTED.

